From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:38:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 208/210] v4l2codecs: Add AVS2 decoder

Add v4l2slavs2dec, a stateless decoder for AVS2 main and main 10
profile video for devices that take the V4L2_PIX_FMT_AVS2_FRAME coded
format, such as the Rockchip VDPU381 (rkvdec) and the Allwinner
cedrus.

Each picture is passed whole, from its picture start code to the end
of its last slice, with the AVS2_SEQUENCE, AVS2_PICTURE,
AVS2_WEIGHT_QUANT (the matrices resolved for the picture) and AVS2_ALF
controls. The output bit depth is the encoding precision of the
sequence, so 8-bit content coded with 10-bit precision is output as
10-bit pictures.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecavs2dec.c | 1068 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
